ld64: keep a branch's offset exactly once when it goes through islands

A branch to a target plus an offset (e.g. `b restGPRx+60`, libgcc's
out-of-line restore of r28-r31, which GCC uses in PowerPC epilogues) that
needs a branch island was broken twice over:

- the branch was redirected to the island but kept its addend, so it
  landed `offset` bytes past the island, in whichever island came next;
- the last island in a chain branched to the target itself, dropping the
  offset, so restGPRx restored registers the function never saved.

In WebKit's WebCore (bigger than PowerPC's +/-32MB branch reach) the first
made a function loop forever and the second corrupted callers' registers.
Now the branch goes to the island with no addend and the island adds it.
Also fixes the shortcut that skips intermediate islands when the final
target is in reach, whose condition could never be true.

